.TH LIBRDP-WORKSPACE 7 "2026-07-15" "librdp 0.1.0" "Miscellaneous Information Manual"
.SH NAME
librdp-workspace \- workspace feed discovery with librdp
.SH DESCRIPTION
The workspace API loads Remote Desktop workspace feeds and exposes published desktop or RemoteApp resources through borrowed resource views.
.P
The API is independent from a live RDP session. Applications can fetch a feed over HTTP(S) with
.BR librdp_workspace_fetch ()
or parse XML obtained by another component with
.BR librdp_workspace_load_xml ().
.SH OBJECTS
.TP
.B librdp_workspace_config
Versioned configuration. The feed URL, username, password, and domain are copied during workspace creation. Password storage is cleared when the workspace is freed.
.TP
.B librdp_workspace
Opaque handle that owns the copied configuration and parsed resources.
.TP
.B librdp_workspace_resource
Borrowed view of one resource. String pointers remain valid until the next workspace fetch, XML load, clear, or free operation.
.SH FUNCTIONS
.TP
.B librdp_workspace_config_init()
Initializes a configuration with default timeout and NULL optional strings.
.TP
.B librdp_workspace_new()
Creates a workspace handle from a configuration.
.TP
.B librdp_workspace_fetch()
Fetches the configured HTTP(S) feed and parses resources. It returns
.B LIBRDP_STATUS_UNSUPPORTED
when the HTTP or XML backend is not compiled.
.TP
.B librdp_workspace_load_xml()
Parses caller-provided XML bytes. It returns
.B LIBRDP_STATUS_UNSUPPORTED
when XML parsing support is not compiled.
.TP
.B librdp_workspace_resource_count()
Returns the number of parsed resources.
.TP
.B librdp_workspace_resource_at()
Copies a borrowed view of one parsed resource into a caller-owned structure.
.SH SECURITY
Workspace feed data is untrusted input. Applications should validate launch metadata and apply their own policy before starting an RDP session from feed contents.
.P
Feed credentials must not be logged. Trace events for workspace fetches report redacted metadata only.
.SH EXAMPLE
The
.B librdp-example-workspace-list
example loads a feed URL or XML file and prints the normalized resource list.
.P
The
.BR librdp-x11-workspace (1)
tool uses the same API to fetch a feed, select a resource, and start the X11 viewer.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR librdp (7),
.BR librdp-api (7),
.BR librdp-x11-workspace (1)
